     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Here is how to weave a branch:\n\n- Gather the threads\n  1. Pick a node\n  2. Draw three continuations\n- Compare them side by side\n\nA short example:\n\n```js\nconst loom = weave('aspen');\nloom.branch(3);\n```\n\nThe paragraph after the code block.\n\n1. Numbered outer\n   - a bullet inside\n2. Second step"
      }
     ],
     "author": {
      "role": "model",
      "name": "anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5"
     },
     "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:01.000Z"
    },
    "m-1b": {
     "id": "m-1b",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "## Aspen at a glance\n\nA **quaking aspen** grove is often *one* plant.\n\n| Trait | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Root system | `shared` |\n| Age | thousands of years |"
      }
     ],
     "author": {
      "role": "model",
      "name": "anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5"
     },
     "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:02.000Z"
    },
    "m-2": {
     "id": "m-2",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "And inline styles mid-sentence?"
      }
     ],
     "author": {
      "role": "human"
     },
     "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:03.000Z"
    },
    "m-3": {
     "id": "m-3",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Quaking aspen spreads by suckering. The clonal **root system shared underground** can survive fire, drought and *centuries of hard mountain winters*, so a single grove can be one organism, and `loom.branch(3)` draws three continuations in one call.\n\n- **Connected roots:** every stem in the grove draws water from one shared network of roots.\n\n| Call | Returns |\n| --- | --- |\n| `loom.branch(3)` | `void`, not the *original* node |\n\nA wide command:\n\n```sh\nnode scripts/seed-perf-tree/cli.ts --seed 1 --model anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5 --price-in 1 --price-out 5 --yes  # END-OF-LINE\n```"
      }
     ],
     "author": {
      "role": "model",
      "name": "anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5"
     },
     "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:04.000Z"
    }
